{"name":"Garter belt","deep":true,"image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e6/Garter_belt_%28drawing%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Garter_belt_(drawing).jpg","caption":"Garter belt (drawing)","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},"mentions":0,"casual":{"lead":["A garter belt (a suspender belt in British English) is a wide elasticated band worn at or just below the waist with two or three elastic straps on each side. Metal clips attach to the tops of stockings, holding them up without a band squeezing the thigh.","Its looks payoff is styling: a clean, smooth stocking line, a fitted waist look under clothing and a vintage or formal silhouette. It descends from older garters tied below the knee."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["The belt is worn at or just below the waist so it does not slide down under the pull of the stockings; the clips grip the stocking tops. People wear it with stockings for formal, vintage or costume looks, and with medical support hosiery."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["Poor fit can cause pressure marks or slipping. Doctors sometimes suggest stockings with suspenders instead of tights for people prone to yeast or urinary infections [1]."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e6/Garter_belt_%28drawing%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e6/Garter_belt_%28drawing%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Garter belt (drawing)","license":"CC0","creator":"David Ring","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Garter_belt_(drawing).jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Garter_belt.jpg/960px-Garter_belt.jpg?utm_sou